# The Node floor is enforced by CI, which runs the version `.nvmrc` names and
# blocks a merge when it fails. That is the gate.
#
# `engine-strict=true` lived here for a day and its first victim was Dependabot:
# the updater runs pnpm in its own container on its own Node, the install failed
# with ERR_PNPM_UNSUPPORTED_ENGINE, and Dependabot read that as "these
# dependencies are no longer updatable" and closed its pull request — while the
# updates it wanted were sitting on the registry. A gate that stops the repo
# maintaining itself is not paying for its own upkeep, so `engines.node` is back
# to being a statement to humans, and CI is what refuses.
#
# If a local refusal is ever wanted again, `use-node-version` is the setting that
# achieves it without locking anything out: pnpm provisions the named Node
# instead of declining to run.
